ing out of position, it is generally safer to keep the pot small pre-flop unless you have a premium hand.\n\nReason: Checking allows you to see the flop for free to realize your hand's equity (flush or straight potential) without bloating the pot while out of position. Raising creates a larger pot where you are at a disadvantage if called, especially with a weak kicker.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
