alling a pot-sized bet out of position with only Ace-high and no direct draws is a losing play in the long run.\n\nReason:\nYou hold a weak hand with limited improvement potential (backdoor flush draw and overcards with a weak kicker) on a board that favors the aggressor or random hands that connected with the 6 or 9. The opponent's bet size indicates strength or a committed bluff, and without a made hand or strong draw, conserving chips for a better opportunity is the optimal strategy.\n\nAnswer: -1"}
